        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Rhymers' Club\n- People: W. B. Yeats, Ernest Rhys, Herbert Horne\n- Places: London, Ye Olde Cheshire Cheese, Café Royal, Fleet Street, Wine Office Court, City of London\n\nFacts:\n- In 1890, W. B. Yeats and Ernest Rhys founded the Rhymers' Club.\n- The Rhymers' Club was a group of London-based male poets.\n- The Rhymers' Club met at Ye Olde Cheshire Cheese in Fleet Street and in the Domino Room of the Café Royal.\n- Ye Olde Cheshire Cheese is a Grade II listed public house at 145 Fleet Street on Wine Office Court in the City of London.\n- Herbert Horne was an associate of the Rhymers' Club in London.",
